Tithe was a [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] the size of a planet, bluish gray and almost entirely land, with no seas worth the name. It curled in on itself at one end as if a fissure had been cut through it. Advanced peoples lived on and around it and worshipped it, and they ringed it with barriers that turned aside ships and kept anyone from landing on its body.

The [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Harrow|Harrow]] killed Tithe and set about devouring the body. [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] raced to strip some of the divine essence out of it before the Harrow swallowed it all. A beacon planted on the surface let its fleet take a third of the world away in a beam of light, and the ships fled before the Harrow could turn on them. What was left was eaten.
